# Karai, Future of the Foot. Turn 3: Bot1 attacks with Ornithopter, unblocked, and in the declare blockers step sneaks Karai in for
# {2}{W}{B}, returning the Ornithopter; in response Choreographed Sparks (Lotus' RRR) copies the Karai spell. The copy resolves
# first, a token Karai that enters tapped and attacking (its sneak cost was paid, CR 707.10); then the card Karai, and the legend
# rule keeps the token, the card going to the graveyard. The token deals 3 combat damage: "return target creature card from your
# graveyard to your hand. If her sneak cost was paid this turn, instead return that card to the battlefield" - the Karai card,
# the only creature card there, returns to the battlefield (and the legend rule keeps the token again), not to hand.

